(3,'🟢',"Why do ML models degrade after deployment? Define data drift (covariate shift), concept drift, label or prior shift and an upstream data change, and separate all four from training-serving skew, which is a bug and not a world change. For each say what changes (P(x), P(y|x), P(y)), what you can see without labels and what needs labels. Simulate the four on synthetic data with numpy and a simple scikit-learn classifier, report the feature-drift statistic, the prediction-rate change and the accuracy for each, and show which cases a feature-only monitor misses. Book 1 owns the theory, so keep to what a monitor needs.",QB+" | "+SC),
